# Benchmark artifacts must reproduce byte-for-byte on any checkout.
#
# The repo runs with core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule a fresh clone lands CRLF in the
# working tree while the builders write LF -- re-running Stage 22 on a clean checkout would then
# diff every table for line endings alone. Verified by cloning and comparing.
results/** text eol=lf

# Frozen at Stage 21D with CRLF in the blob. Marked binary so it is neither converted nor
# renormalized: rewriting a frozen 21D artifact is exactly what the no-rewrite rule forbids, and
# its content is identical either way.
results/stage21d_rewind_clone_table.tsv -text

# Binary files are never line-ending converted. `results/** text eol=lf` above forces text handling on
# everything under results/, binaries included: example_clone_expression.npy was committed under that
# rule, and a .docx or .pdf rendered into results/manuscript/submission/ would be corrupted on commit.
# Later lines win, so these override the rule above.
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
